{"id":"mahabharata-5-187","work":"mahabharata","part":5,"partName":"उद्योगपर्व","partNameEn":"Udyoga Parva","unit":187,"title":"सप्ताशीत्यधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 187 · Amba's austerities","summary":{"en":"Amba declares that she will win Bhishma's death by her own austerity, and goes into the forest, practising terrible penances for years, fasting and standing in the waters. By the power of her penance half of her becomes a river, the Amba, and half remains a maiden.","kn":"ತನ್ನ ತಪಸ್ಸಿನಿಂದಲೇ ಭೀಷ್ಮನ ಮರಣ ಗಳಿಸುವೆನೆಂದು ಘೋಷಿಸಿ ಅಂಬೆ ಕಾಡಿಗೆ ಹೋಗಿ ವರ್ಷಗಟ್ಟಲೆ ಉಪವಾಸ, ನೀರಿನಲ್ಲಿ ನಿಲ್ಲುವುದು ಮುಂತಾದ ಘೋರ ತಪಸ್ಸು ಆಚರಿಸುತ್ತಾಳೆ. ತಪಸ್ಸಿನ ಶಕ್ತಿಯಿಂದ ಅವಳ ಅರ್ಧಭಾಗ ಅಂಬಾನದಿಯಾಗುತ್ತದೆ, ಅರ್ಧ ಕನ್ಯೆಯಾಗಿ ಉಳಿಯುತ್ತದೆ.","hi":"अम्बा घोषणा करती है कि वह अपने तप से भीष्म की मृत्यु प्राप्त करेगी, और वन में जाकर वर्षों तक उपवास और जल में खड़े रहने जैसे घोर तप करती है। तप की शक्ति से उसका आधा भाग अम्बा नदी बन जाता है और आधा कन्या रह जाता है।","te":"తన తపస్సుతోనే భీష్ముని మరణాన్ని సాధిస్తానని ప్రకటించి అంబ అడవికి వెళ్లి సంవత్సరాల తరబడి ఉపవాసం, నీటిలో నిలబడడం వంటి ఘోర తపస్సు చేస్తుంది. తపశ్శక్తితో ఆమె సగభాగం అంబానదిగా మారుతుంది, సగం కన్యగా మిగులుతుంది.","ta":"தன் தவத்தாலேயே பீஷ்மரின் சாவைப் பெறுவேன் என்று அறிவித்து அம்பை காட்டுக்குச் சென்று ஆண்டுக்கணக்கில் உண்ணாநோன்பு, நீரில் நிற்றல் போன்ற கடுந்தவம் புரிகிறாள். தவ வலிமையால் அவளில் பாதி அம்பா நதியாக, பாதி கன்னியாக நிலைக்கிறாள்.","ml":"തന്റെ തപസ്സുകൊണ്ട് ഭീഷ്മരുടെ മരണം നേടുമെന്ന് അംബ പ്രഖ്യാപിക്കുന്നു; അവൾ കാട്ടിലേക്ക് പോയി വർഷങ്ങളോളം ഘോരതപസ്സ് അനുഷ്ഠിക്കുന്നു, ഉപവസിച്ചും വെള്ളത്തിൽ നിന്നും. ആ തപസ്സിന്റെ ശക്തിയാൽ അവളുടെ പകുതി അംബ എന്ന നദിയായി മാറുന്നു; പകുതി കന്യകയായി തുടരുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 5.187; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Jan 23 2024","sections":[{"title":"अम्बोपाख्यानपर्व","titleEn":"Ambopakhyana Parva (The story of Amba)","verses":[{"text":"राम उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Rama said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"प्रत्यक्षमेतल्लोकानां सर्वेषामेव भामिनि ।\nयथा मया परं शक्त्या कृतं वै पौरुषं महत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Everyone in the world has seen this, fair lady, how I have shown great manly effort with all my strength."}},{"n":2,"text":"न चैव युधि शक्नोमि भीष्मं शस्त्रभृतां वरम् ।\nविशेषयितुमत्यर्थमुत्तमास्त्राणि दर्शयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Even by displaying my best weapons I could not in battle gain any decisive advantage over Bhishma, the best of weapon-bearers."}},{"n":3,"text":"एषा मे परमा शक्तिरेतन्मे परमं बलम् ।\nयथेष्टं गम्यतां भद्रे किमन्यद्वा करोमि ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"This is my utmost power and my utmost strength. Go where you please, good lady, or what else can I do for you?"}},{"n":4,"text":"भीष्ममेव प्रपद्यस्व न तेऽन्या विद्यते गतिः ।\nनिर्जितो ह्यस्मि भीष्मेण महास्त्राणि प्रमुञ्चता ॥","meaning":{"en":"Take refuge in Bhishma himself; you have no other way. I have been defeated by Bhishma as he released his great weapons."}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":5,"text":"एवमुक्त्वा ततो रामो विनिःश्वस्य महामनाः ।\nतूष्णीमासीत्तदा कन्या प्रोवाच भृगुनन्दनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having said this, great-minded Rama sighed and fell silent. Then the maiden spoke to the son of Bhrigu."}},{"n":6,"text":"भगवन्नेवमेवैतद्यथाह भगवांस्तथा ।\nअजेयो युधि भीष्मोऽयमपि देवैरुदारधीः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Revered one, it is just as you say. Bhishma, noble in mind, cannot be conquered in battle even by the gods.\""}},{"n":7,"text":"यथाशक्ति यथोत्साहं मम कार्यं कृतं त्वया ।\nअनिधाय रणे वीर्यमस्त्राणि विविधानि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"You have done my work as far as your strength and effort allowed, not holding back your might or your many weapons in the fight.\""}},{"n":8,"text":"न चैष शक्यते युद्धे विशेषयितुमन्ततः ।\nन चाहमेनं यास्यामि पुनर्भीष्मं कथंचन ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"He cannot in the end be bested in battle, and I will never go to this Bhishma again.\""}},{"n":9,"text":"गमिष्यामि तु तत्राहं यत्र भीष्मं तपोधन ।\nसमरे पातयिष्यामि स्वयमेव भृगूद्वह ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"But I will go to the place, O ascetic, where I can bring Bhishma down in battle by myself, O best of Bhrigu's line.\""}},{"n":10,"text":"एवमुक्त्वा ययौ कन्या रोषव्याकुललोचना ।\nतपसे धृतसंकल्पा मम चिन्तयती वधम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having said this, the maiden went away, her eyes troubled with anger, firmly resolved on austerity and thinking of my death."}},{"n":11,"text":"ततो महेन्द्रं सह तैर्मुनिभिर्भृगुसत्तमः ।\nयथागतं ययौ रामो मामुपामन्त्र्य भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Rama, best of Bhrigu's line, took leave of me, O Bharata, and went back to Mahendra with those sages, as he had come."}},{"n":12,"text":"ततोऽहं रथमारुह्य स्तूयमानो द्विजातिभिः ।\nप्रविश्य नगरं मात्रे सत्यवत्यै न्यवेदयम् ।\nयथावृत्तं महाराज सा च मां प्रत्यनन्दत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then I mounted my chariot, praised by the twice-born, entered the city, and told my mother Satyavati everything that had happened, O great king; she rejoiced at it."}},{"n":13,"text":"पुरुषांश्चादिशं प्राज्ञान्कन्यावृत्तान्तकर्मणि ।\nदिवसे दिवसे ह्यस्या गतजल्पितचेष्टितम् ।\nप्रत्याहरंश्च मे युक्ताः स्थिताः प्रियहिते मम ॥","meaning":{"en":"I appointed wise men to report on the maiden's doings, and day by day those men, devoted to my welfare, brought me word of her words and actions."}},{"n":14,"text":"यदैव हि वनं प्रायात्कन्या सा तपसे धृता ।\nतदैव व्यथितो दीनो गतचेता इवाभवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"From the moment that maiden went into the forest, set on austerity, I became troubled and wretched, almost out of my senses."}},{"n":15,"text":"न हि मां क्षत्रियः कश्चिद्वीर्येण विजयेद्युधि ।\nऋते ब्रह्मविदस्तात तपसा संशितव्रतात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"For no Kshatriya can beat me in battle by strength, my friend, except a knower of Brahman, firm in his vows and strong in austerity."}},{"n":16,"text":"अपि चैतन्मया राजन्नारदेऽपि निवेदितम् ।\nव्यासे चैव भयात्कार्यं तौ चोभौ मामवोचताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I also reported this matter to Narada and to Vyasa, O king, out of fear, and both of them told me:"}},{"n":17,"text":"न विषादस्त्वया कार्यो भीष्म काशिसुतां प्रति ।\nदैवं पुरुषकारेण को निवर्तितुमुत्सहेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"You must not grieve, Bhishma, over the daughter of the king of Kashi. Who can turn aside fate by human effort?\""}},{"n":18,"text":"सा तु कन्या महाराज प्रविश्याश्रममण्डलम् ।\nयमुनातीरमाश्रित्य तपस्तेपेऽतिमानुषम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"That maiden, O great king, entered a circle of hermitages and, staying on the bank of the Yamuna, practiced superhuman austerities."}},{"n":19,"text":"निराहारा कृशा रूक्षा जटिला मलपङ्किनी ।\nषण्मासान्वायुभक्षा च स्थाणुभूता तपोधना ॥","meaning":{"en":"Without food, thin, rough, with matted hair and covered in dirt, that ascetic lived on air for six months, standing still like a post."}},{"n":20,"text":"यमुनातीरमासाद्य संवत्सरमथापरम् ।\nउदवासं निराहारा पारयामास भामिनी ॥","meaning":{"en":"Coming to the Yamuna's bank, the lady then spent another year standing in the water without eating."}},{"n":21,"text":"शीर्णपर्णेन चैकेन पारयामास चापरम् ।\nसंवत्सरं तीव्रकोपा पादाङ्गुष्ठाग्रधिष्ठिता ॥","meaning":{"en":"For another year, filled with fierce anger, she lived on a single fallen leaf, standing on the tip of her big toe."}},{"n":22,"text":"एवं द्वादश वर्षाणि तापयामास रोदसी ।\nनिवर्त्यमानापि तु सा ज्ञातिभिर्नैव शक्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"For twelve years she thus scorched heaven and earth, and her relatives could not turn her back."}},{"n":23,"text":"ततोऽगमद्वत्सभूमिं सिद्धचारणसेविताम् ।\nआश्रमं पुण्यशीलानां तापसानां महात्मनाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then she went to the land of the Vatsas, frequented by Siddhas and Charanas, to the hermitage of great ascetics of holy conduct."}},{"n":24,"text":"तत्र पुण्येषु देशेषु साप्लुताङ्गी दिवानिशम् ।\nव्यचरत्काशिकन्या सा यथाकामविचारिणी ॥","meaning":{"en":"In those holy places the Kashi princess bathed day and night and wandered as she wished."}},{"n":25,"text":"नन्दाश्रमे महाराज ततोलूकाश्रमे शुभे ।\nच्यवनस्याश्रमे चैव ब्रह्मणः स्थान एव च ॥","meaning":{"en":"She went to Nanda's hermitage, then the lovely hermitage of Uluka, Chyavana's hermitage, and Brahma's abode, O great king."}},{"n":26,"text":"प्रयागे देवयजने देवारण्येषु चैव ह ।\nभोगवत्यां तथा राजन्कौशिकस्याश्रमे तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"She went to Prayaga, the sacrificial ground of the gods, the forests of the gods, Bhogavati, and the hermitage of Kaushika, O king."}},{"n":27,"text":"माण्डव्यस्याश्रमे राजन्दिलीपस्याश्रमे तथा ।\nरामह्रदे च कौरव्य पैलगार्ग्यस्य चाश्रमे ॥","meaning":{"en":"She went to Mandavya's hermitage, Dilipa's hermitage, Rama's lake, and the hermitage of Paila and Gargya, O Kuru."}},{"n":28,"text":"एतेषु तीर्थेषु तदा काशिकन्या विशां पते ।\nआप्लावयत गात्राणि तीव्रमास्थाय वै तपः ॥","meaning":{"en":"At those holy places, O lord of men, the Kashi princess bathed her limbs and kept up fierce austerity."}},{"n":29,"text":"तामब्रवीत्कौरवेय मम माता जलोत्थिता ।\nकिमर्थं क्लिश्यसे भद्रे तथ्यमेतद्ब्रवीहि मे ॥","meaning":{"en":"O Kuru, my mother, rising from the water, said to her: \"Why do you torment yourself, good lady? Tell me the truth.\""}},{"n":30,"text":"सैनामथाब्रवीद्राजन्कृताञ्जलिरनिन्दिता ।\nभीष्मो रामेण समरे न जितश्चारुलोचने ॥","meaning":{"en":"With folded hands, the blameless maiden answered her, O king: \"Bhishma was not conquered in battle by Rama, fair-eyed lady.\""}},{"n":31,"text":"कोऽन्यस्तमुत्सहेज्जेतुमुद्यतेषुं महीपतिम् ।\nसाहं भीष्मविनाशाय तपस्तप्स्ये सुदारुणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"What other king would dare to defeat him with his arrow raised? So I will practice terrible austerity to destroy Bhishma.\""}},{"n":32,"text":"चरामि पृथिवीं देवि यथा हन्यामहं नृपम् ।\nएतद्व्रतफलं देहे परस्मिन्स्याद्यथा हि मे ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I wander the earth, goddess, so that I may kill that king. Let this vow's fruit come to me in my next body.\""}},{"n":33,"text":"ततोऽब्रवीत्सागरगा जिह्मं चरसि भामिनि ।\nनैष कामोऽनवद्याङ्गि शक्यः प्राप्तुं त्वयाबले ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the goddess who goes to the sea said: \"You are following a crooked course, lady. You cannot reach this desire, weak girl.\""}},{"n":34,"text":"यदि भीष्मविनाशाय काश्ये चरसि वै व्रतम् ।\nव्रतस्था च शरीरं त्वं यदि नाम विमोक्ष्यसि ।\nनदी भविष्यसि शुभे कुटिला वार्षिकोदका ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"If, princess of Kashi, you keep this vow to destroy Bhishma, and if you give up your body while on it, you will become a river, a crooked one with water only in the rains.\""}},{"n":35,"text":"दुस्तीर्था चानभिज्ञेया वार्षिकी नाष्टमासिकी ।\nभीमग्राहवती घोरा सर्वभूतभयंकरी ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Hard to cross, hard to know, flowing in the rainy season and not for eight months, full of dreadful crocodiles, terrible, a fear to all creatures.\""}},{"n":36,"text":"एवमुक्त्वा ततो राजन्काशिकन्यां न्यवर्तत ।\nमाता मम महाभागा स्मयमानेव भामिनी ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having said this, my glorious mother, smiling as it were, turned away from the Kashi princess, O king."}},{"n":37,"text":"कदाचिदष्टमे मासि कदाचिद्दशमे तथा ।\nन प्राश्नीतोदकमपि पुनः सा वरवर्णिनी ॥","meaning":{"en":"But she never again drank water, sometimes through the eighth month, sometimes through the tenth."}},{"n":38,"text":"सा वत्सभूमिं कौरव्य तीर्थलोभात्ततस्ततः ।\nपतिता परिधावन्ती पुनः काशिपतेः सुता ॥","meaning":{"en":"Running here and there in the land of the Vatsas out of desire for holy places, the daughter of the king of Kashi would fall down again and again, O Kuru."}},{"n":39,"text":"सा नदी वत्सभूम्यां तु प्रथिताम्बेति भारत ।\nवार्षिकी ग्राहबहुला दुस्तीर्था कुटिला तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"In the land of the Vatsas that river became famous as Amba, O Bharata, full of crocodiles, hard to cross and crooked, flowing in the rainy season."}},{"n":40,"text":"सा कन्या तपसा तेन भागार्धेन व्यजायत ।\nनदी च राजन्वत्सेषु कन्या चैवाभवत्तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"By that austerity the maiden was born in two halves: she became a river among the Vatsas, and also a maiden."}}]}]}